{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-129100" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(8,-3,5)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-⟨7,-2,4⟩)\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,6⟩=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129100" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(7,-2,4).$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨7,-2,4⟩-⟨8,-3,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-2,-3,6⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-1)\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot (-3)+(-1)\\cdot 6|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2-3-6|}{\\sqrt{4+9+36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-7|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{7} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129100" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "335dda9e71a7fab766ef87251edb2978d4ed00a23de77d03429ef970518aba06"} {"question" "q-129100" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129100" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129100" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129096" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-3,1,4)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-⟨3,-2,1⟩)\\cdot ⟨-2,4,-4⟩=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129096" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(3,-2,1).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨3,-2,1⟩-⟨-3,1,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,-3,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-2,4,-4⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|6\\cdot (-2)+(-3)\\cdot 4+(-3)\\cdot (-4)|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-12|}{\\sqrt{4+16+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-12|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129096" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "335dda9e71a7fab766ef87251edb2978d4ed00a23de77d03429ef970518aba06"} {"question" "q-129096" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129096" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{11}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{13}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129096" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-33466" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(3,5,-2)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-33466" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(5,9,0).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2\\cdot (-2)+4\\cdot 2+2\\cdot (-4)|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-4+8-8|}{\\sqrt{4+4+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-4|}{\\sqrt{24}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-33466" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "335dda9e71a7fab766ef87251edb2978d4ed00a23de77d03429ef970518aba06"} {"question" "q-33466" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-33466" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-33466" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-34031" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-1,2,-3)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-⟨1,-5,3⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,0,4⟩=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-34031" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(1,-5,3).$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,-5,3⟩-⟨-1,2,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-7,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨1,0,4⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2\\cdot 1+(-7)\\cdot 0+6\\cdot 4|}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2+0+24|}{\\sqrt{1+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|26|}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\  & =\\frac{26\\sqrt{17}}{17}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-34031" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "335dda9e71a7fab766ef87251edb2978d4ed00a23de77d03429ef970518aba06"} {"question" "q-34031" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-34031" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "\\frac{19\\sqrt{17}}{17}"] ["math" "\\frac{23\\sqrt{17}}{17}"] ["math" "\\frac{26\\sqrt{17}}{17}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-34031" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{26\\sqrt{17}}{17}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129095" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(5,2,2)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129095" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(2,-1,1).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-3)\\cdot 4+(-3)\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 4|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-12-6-4|}{\\sqrt{16+4+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-22|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129095" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "335dda9e71a7fab766ef87251edb2978d4ed00a23de77d03429ef970518aba06"} {"question" "q-129095" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129095" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{11}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{13}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129095" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{11}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-34074" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $Q(2,4,1)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨-6,2,9⟩=5$, find the shortest distance from $P(6,-1,0)$ to $Π.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-34074" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,4,1⟩-⟨6,-1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,5,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-6,2,9⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-4)\\cdot (-6)+5\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 9|}{\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{9}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|24+10+9|}{\\sqrt{36+4+81}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|43|}{\\sqrt{121}} \\\\  & =\\frac{43}{11}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-34074" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "335dda9e71a7fab766ef87251edb2978d4ed00a23de77d03429ef970518aba06"} {"question" "q-34074" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-34074" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{11\\sqrt{26}}{13}"] ["math" "\\frac{43}{11}"] ["math" "\\frac{48}{11}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-34074" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{43}{11}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129102" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $Q(4,-2,8)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨-3,6,2⟩=-8$, find the shortest distance from $P(3,-4,2)$ to $Π.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129102" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨4,-2,8⟩-⟨3,-4,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,2,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-3,6,2⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|1\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot 6+6\\cdot 2|}{\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{6}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-3+12+12|}{\\sqrt{9+36+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|21|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{21}{7} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129102" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "335dda9e71a7fab766ef87251edb2978d4ed00a23de77d03429ef970518aba06"} {"question" "q-129102" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129102" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129102" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-80049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $Q(1,3,4)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨-4,2,0⟩=2$, find the shortest distance from $P(5,-2,3)$ to $Π.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-80049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,3,4⟩-⟨5,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,5,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-4,2,0⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-4)\\cdot (-4)+5\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 0|}{\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|16+10+0|}{\\sqrt{16+4+0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|26|}{\\sqrt{20}} \\\\  & =\\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-80049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "335dda9e71a7fab766ef87251edb2978d4ed00a23de77d03429ef970518aba06"} {"question" "q-80049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-80049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "13\\sqrt{20}"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{13}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-80049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-34075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $Q(1,3,5)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨-4,1,-3⟩=-16$, find the shortest distance from $P(-3,7,3)$ to $Π.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-34075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,3,5⟩-⟨-3,7,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,-4,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-4,1,-3⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|4\\cdot (-4)+(-4)\\cdot 1+2\\cdot (-3)|}{\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-16-4-6|}{\\sqrt{16+1+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-26|}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{26}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-34075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "335dda9e71a7fab766ef87251edb2978d4ed00a23de77d03429ef970518aba06"} {"question" "q-34075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-34075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "\\frac{3\\sqrt{26}}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{26}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{26}}{3}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{26}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-34075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{26}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129148" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(5,3,7)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $r\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,6⟩=16.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129148" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=⟨x,y,z⟩,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,6⟩ & =16 \\\\ -2x-3y+6z & =16 \\\\ 2x & =6z-3y-16 \\\\ x & =3z-\\frac{3}{2}y-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $y=2$ and $z=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nx=3-\\frac{3}{2}(2)-8=-8.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(-8,2,1)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨-8,2,1⟩-⟨5,3,7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-13,-1,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-2,-3,6⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-13)\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot (-3)+(-6)\\cdot 6|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|26+3-36|}{\\sqrt{4+9+36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-7|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{7} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129148" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "335dda9e71a7fab766ef87251edb2978d4ed00a23de77d03429ef970518aba06"} {"question" "q-129148" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129148" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{10}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129148" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-2,3,-6)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $-x+2y+2z=8.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=-2$ and $y=1$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+2y+2z & =8 \\\\ -1(-2)+2(1)+2z & =8 \\\\ 2z & =4 \\\\ z & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(-2,1,2)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨-2,1,2⟩-⟨-2,3,-6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-2,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨-1,2,2⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|0\\cdot (-1)+(-2)\\cdot 2+8\\cdot 2|}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|0-4+16|}{\\sqrt{1+4+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|12|}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{3} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "335dda9e71a7fab766ef87251edb2978d4ed00a23de77d03429ef970518aba06"} {"question" "q-129166" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129166" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129166" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-2,1,5)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $-2x+4y+4z=18.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=-1$ and $y=2$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+4y+4z & =18 \\\\ -2(-1)+4(2)+4z & =18 \\\\ 4z & =8 \\\\ z & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(-1,2,2)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨-1,2,2⟩-⟨-2,1,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,1,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨-2,4,4⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|1\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot 4+(-3)\\cdot 4|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-2+4-12|}{\\sqrt{4+16+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-10|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "335dda9e71a7fab766ef87251edb2978d4ed00a23de77d03429ef970518aba06"} {"question" "q-129160" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129160" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{11}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-129160" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-80122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-1,11,10)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $-2x-4y+4z=16.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-80122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=2$ and $y=3$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x-4y+4z & =16 \\\\ -2(2)-4(3)+4z & =16 \\\\ 4z & =32 \\\\ z & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(2,3,8)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,3,8⟩-⟨-1,11,10⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-8,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨-2,-4,4⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|3\\cdot (-2)+(-8)\\cdot (-4)+(-2)\\cdot 4|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-6+32-8|}{\\sqrt{4+16+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,18\\,|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-80122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "335dda9e71a7fab766ef87251edb2978d4ed00a23de77d03429ef970518aba06"} {"question" "q-80122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-80122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "18"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-80122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-80120" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-11,-8,-4)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $14x+8y-8z=-6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-80120" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=-1$ and $y=-2$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14x+8y-8z & =-6 \\\\ 14(-1)+8(-2)-8z & =-6 \\\\ -8z & =24 \\\\ z & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(-1,-2,-3)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨-1,-2,-3⟩-⟨-11,-8,-4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨10,6,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨14,8,-8⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|10\\cdot 14+6\\cdot 8+1\\cdot (-8)|}{\\sqrt{(14)^{2}+{8}^{2}+(-8)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|140+48-8|}{\\sqrt{196+64+64}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,180\\,|}{\\sqrt{324}} \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-80120" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "335dda9e71a7fab766ef87251edb2978d4ed00a23de77d03429ef970518aba06"} {"question" "q-80120" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-80120" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "18"] ["math" "\\sqrt{15}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-80120" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-80119" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(6,6,2)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $4x-7y-4z=-26.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-80119" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=2$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-7y-4z & =-26 \\\\ 4(1)-7(2)-4z & =-26 \\\\ -4z & =-16 \\\\ z & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,2,4)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,2,4⟩-⟨6,6,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,-4,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨4,-7,-4⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-5)\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot (-7)+2\\cdot (-4)|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-7)^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-20+28-8|}{\\sqrt{16+49+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,0\\,|}{\\sqrt{81}} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $P$ lies on the plane." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-80119" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "335dda9e71a7fab766ef87251edb2978d4ed00a23de77d03429ef970518aba06"} {"question" "q-80119" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-80119" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "3\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "9"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "q-80119" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3573f7afb132288f6215698e879a302247da1f8668888d1c077811f04884cee"} {"question" "e-4949" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(5,2,-2)$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equation ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/assets/40ec5f2b2615eedf6b16420a2089b7c377141db46237de35218c5e685b629918.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/example-4949.json" "file_sha256" "2f021ae9e8da5034718eb4af4830369345eccaae8ad409d872f68a72d5f1e472"} {"question" "e-4949" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(4,8,2).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/assets/0589ebbdb2c14b93e1296b9e1f8b0caa0c3df49bff4c9fbb97e4c18102844ec1.png)\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-1)\\cdot 2+6\\cdot 4+4\\cdot (-4)|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-2+24-16|}{\\sqrt{4+16+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,6\\,|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/example-4949.json" "file_sha256" "2f021ae9e8da5034718eb4af4830369345eccaae8ad409d872f68a72d5f1e472"} {"question" "e-4950" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $Q(1,-2,-1)$ lies on the plane $\\Pi:\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle 2, 0, -2 \\rangle = 4,$ find the shortest distance from $P(0 , -1 , 2)$ to $\\Pi.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/example-4950.json" "file_sha256" "d4b188c4a0da07111ace1a3a3770395e7cd1b4e70c295ceebaa28d2b6bb804aa"} {"question" "e-4950" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,-2,-1⟩-⟨0,-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $\\mathbf{n}= \\langle 2, 0, -2 \\rangle.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|1\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2+0+6|}{\\sqrt{4+0+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,8\\,|}{\\sqrt{8}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/example-4950.json" "file_sha256" "d4b188c4a0da07111ace1a3a3770395e7cd1b4e70c295ceebaa28d2b6bb804aa"} {"question" "e-4951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(3 , -10 , 3)$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equation $2x+y-2z = -1$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/example-4951.json" "file_sha256" "7ff97404880265c7c245873147e46cd6a6814b1e097fc7dfc95c75c3f66f6d11"} {"question" "e-4951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=4$ and $y=-5$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+y-2z & =-1 \\\\ 2(4)+(-5)+1 & =2z \\\\ 4 & =2z \\\\ z & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(4, -5, 2)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overrightarrow{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨4,-5,2⟩-⟨3,-10,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,5,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle a,b,c \\rangle.$ So, for the plane $\\Pi,$ we have $\\mathbf{n}= \\langle 2, 1, -2 \\rangle.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|1\\cdot 2+5\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2+5+2|}{\\sqrt{4+1+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,9\\,|}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/example-4951.json" "file_sha256" "7ff97404880265c7c245873147e46cd6a6814b1e097fc7dfc95c75c3f66f6d11"}] "usage" {"q-33466" [] "e-4949" [] "e-4951" [] "q-34031" [] "q-34075" [] "e-4950" []} "basis" 1930 "retractions" [[17592186120184 :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(3, 5,-2)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r - \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}) \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} = 0$."] [17592186120225 :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-1, 2,-3)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r - ⟨1,-5, 3⟩) \\cdot ⟨1, 0, 4⟩ = 0$."] [17592186120230 :question/problem "Given that $Q(1, 3, 5)$ lies on the plane $Π: r \\cdot ⟨ - 4, 1,-3⟩ =-16$, find the shortest distance from $P(-3, 7, 3)$ to $Π$."] [17592186119580 :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(5,2,-2)$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equation $\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186119580 :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(4,8,2)$. Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nPQ^(→) &= \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nd &= \\mid comp_{n}PQ^(→) \\mid \\\\\n&= (\\begin{vmatrix}PQ^(→) \\cdot n &)/(\\mid n\\end{vmatrix}) \\\\\n&= (\\mid (-1) \\cdot 2 + 6 \\cdot 4 + 4 \\cdot (-4)\\begin{vmatrix})/(\\sqrt{2^{2} + 4^{2} + (-4)^{2}}) \\\\ = \\frac{\\mid - 2 + 24 - 16 \\mid}{\\sqrt{4 + 16 + 16}} \\\\ = \\frac{\\mid 6\\end{vmatrix}}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\\n&= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186119581 :question/problem "Given that $Q(1,-2,-1)$ lies on the plane $\\Pi:\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle 2, 0, -2 \\rangle = 4$, find the shortest distance from $P(0, -1, 2)$ to $\\Pi$."] [17592186119581 :question/worked-solution "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nPQ^(→) &= ⟨1,-2,-1⟩ - ⟨0,-1, 2⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨1,-1,-3⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}= \\langle 2, 0, -2 \\rangle\n$$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nd &= \\mid comp_{n}PQ^(→) \\mid \\\\\n&= (\\begin{vmatrix}PQ^(→) \\cdot n &)/(\\mid n\\end{vmatrix}) \\\\\n&= (\\mid 1 \\cdot 2 + (-1) \\cdot 0 + (-3) \\cdot (-2)\\begin{vmatrix})/(\\sqrt{2^{2} + 0^{2} + (-2)^{2}}) \\\\ = \\frac{\\mid 2 + 0 + 6 \\mid}{\\sqrt{4 + 0 + 4}} \\\\ = \\frac{\\mid 8\\end{vmatrix}}{\\sqrt{8}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{8} \\\\\n&= 2\\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186119582 :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(3, -10, 3)$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equation $2x+y-2z = -1$."] [17592186119582 :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z$. Let's choose $x=4$ and $y=-5$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x + y - 2z &= -1 \\\\\n2(4) + (-5) + 1 &= 2z \\\\\n4 &= 2z \\\\\nz &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(4, -5, 2)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nPQ^(→) &= ⟨4,-5, 2⟩ - ⟨3,-10, 3⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨1, 5,-1⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane\n\n$$\nax+by+cz=d\n$$\n\nthe normal vector is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}=\\langle a,b,c \\rangle\n$$\n\nSo, for the plane $\\Pi$, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}= \\langle 2, 1, -2 \\rangle\n$$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nd &= \\mid comp_{n}PQ^(→) \\mid \\\\\n&= (\\begin{vmatrix}PQ^(→) \\cdot n &)/(\\mid n\\end{vmatrix}) \\\\\n&= (\\mid 1 \\cdot 2 + 5 \\cdot 1 + (-1) \\cdot (-2)\\begin{vmatrix})/(\\sqrt{2^{2} + 1^{2} + (-2)^{2}}) \\\\ = \\frac{\\mid 2 + 5 + 2 \\mid}{\\sqrt{4 + 1 + 4}} \\\\ = \\frac{\\mid 9\\end{vmatrix}}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\\n&= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186117625 17592186117626 17592186117627 17592186117628 17592186117629 17592186117851 17592186117852 17592186117853 17592186117854 17592186117855 17592186117881 17592186117882 17592186117883 17592186117884 17592186117885] "immutable_fields" [[17592186117624 :answer-field/correct] [17592186117624 :answer-field/id] [17592186117624 :answer-field/key] [17592186117624 :answer-field/type] [17592186117850 :answer-field/correct] [17592186117850 :answer-field/id] [17592186117850 :answer-field/key] [17592186117850 :answer-field/type] [17592186117880 :answer-field/correct] [17592186117880 :answer-field/id] [17592186117880 :answer-field/key] [17592186117880 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
